WEBVTT

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:06.678
Gentle-hearted gay man Genichi Hatano

00:00:06.744 --> 00:00:07.679
is chasing love.

00:00:07.745 --> 00:00:08.580
I like you!

00:00:08.646 --> 00:00:09.514
‎PREVIOUSLY ON ‎CHOSEN HOME

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:11.916
His love interest was fresh off a breakup,

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:13.351
a middle school teacher, Saku Sakuta.

00:00:13.418 --> 00:00:15.086
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:00:15.153 --> 00:00:17.655
Saku’s troublesome student,
Hotaru Kusunoki,

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:19.657
offered 30 million yen
embezzled by her mom,

00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:21.559
pleading Genichi to pose as her dad.

00:00:21.626 --> 00:00:24.996
But when Hotaru’s real dad shows up
for the money…

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:26.231
I'm her dad.

00:00:26.297 --> 00:00:27.932
A gay person calling himself
a dad is weird.

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:29.801
It's not weird at all!

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.504
I borrowed an empty unit.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.405
I support you
in pretending to be her parent.

00:00:34.472 --> 00:00:37.675
Now, with Saku drawn into the fake family,

00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:39.444
Genichi’s love life takes off!

00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:42.013
Convince him it’s fate.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.615
Yeah, it's fate.

00:00:43.681 --> 00:00:46.651
Meanwhile, Hotaru’s mother, Tomoe,
who’s on the run,

00:00:46.718 --> 00:00:49.120
sends out a letter addressed to…

00:00:49.954 --> 00:00:50.655
PORK MISO SOUP AND RICE BALLS
FOOD DISTRIBUTION SITE

00:00:50.722 --> 00:00:52.557
We're distributing free samples!

00:00:52.624 --> 00:00:54.826
‎Please take your time
‎and move forward in line.

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:56.261
Here you go.

00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:02.133
Do you know it tastes better
if you add true mirin?

00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:05.203
To miso soup. It makes the flavor milder.

00:01:06.104 --> 00:01:07.405
I’ll have some ready next time.

00:01:08.139 --> 00:01:10.108
Really? Thank you so much.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.012
Hey, hey.

00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:15.780
is true mirin added in this?

00:01:15.847 --> 00:01:17.081
No.

00:01:17.148 --> 00:01:18.917
Come on. That’s the least you could do!

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.454
Is it a trend now?

00:01:24.055 --> 00:01:26.658
-Sorry to trouble you with so much stuff.
-No worries.

00:01:27.358 --> 00:01:29.961
We’re officially neighbors now.

00:01:30.028 --> 00:01:32.630
Guess so.

00:01:34.465 --> 00:01:35.400
Um…

00:01:36.935 --> 00:01:39.304
If I ever make too much food,
I’ll bring some over.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.307
You sound all too prepared to doing that.

00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:43.208
Not at all.

00:01:43.274 --> 00:01:45.577
The car is getting cramped,

00:01:45.643 --> 00:01:48.413
and I want to take my time
finding a new place, hence I moved in.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:49.881
Right.

00:01:49.948 --> 00:01:51.683
Once your furniture arrives, I’ll help

00:01:51.749 --> 00:01:52.850
put it together.

00:01:53.685 --> 00:01:55.153
You sure you should be doing that?

00:01:55.887 --> 00:01:57.522
-Huh?
-Hotaru.

00:01:58.189 --> 00:02:00.391
Her finals start tomorrow.

00:02:10.101 --> 00:02:11.336
What do you want?

00:02:12.203 --> 00:02:14.872
-I heard you’ve got exams coming up.
-Yeah.

00:02:14.939 --> 00:02:16.507
Whatever career you decide on,

00:02:16.574 --> 00:02:18.142
isn't it better to study for it?

00:02:18.209 --> 00:02:19.177
I hate tests.

00:02:19.244 --> 00:02:21.746
-You still gotta take them.
-Why?

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.915
For your future.

00:02:23.982 --> 00:02:25.883
Do I even have one?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.518
Shall I help you study?

00:02:28.253 --> 00:02:29.320
You're annoying.

00:02:42.166 --> 00:02:44.202
-You sure I can come in?
-You said you'll help.

00:02:44.269 --> 00:02:46.604
-Well then.
-Wait!

00:02:48.039 --> 00:02:49.407
Wipe your feet first.

00:02:52.577 --> 00:02:54.345
Okay, let’s start with a question.

00:02:54.412 --> 00:02:56.748
The test is gonna have stuff
that’s not in the textbook.

00:02:56.814 --> 00:02:57.715
What?

00:02:57.782 --> 00:02:59.651
Your teacher is really mean, huh?

00:02:59.717 --> 00:03:01.452
It's Mr. Sakuta, though.

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:03.554
I'm sure some of it will be from the book.

00:03:04.289 --> 00:03:06.224
-Who knows?
-Okay, next.

00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:09.193
"When the Moon passes
between the Earth and the Sun

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.596
and the Sun is completely hidden
by the Moon,

00:03:11.663 --> 00:03:15.300
what’s that phenomenon called?"

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:16.934
Despair.

00:03:17.502 --> 00:03:19.237
Well, it does get dark,

00:03:19.304 --> 00:03:21.606
so you may feel that way,

00:03:21.673 --> 00:03:23.207
but it's called "total solar eclipse".

00:03:23.274 --> 00:03:27.178
Next question. "The next
total solar eclipse visible in Japan

00:03:27.245 --> 00:03:29.847
will be in what year?"

00:03:30.782 --> 00:03:32.116
Some ridiculously far-off year.

00:03:33.451 --> 00:03:36.120
You're right, but the answer is year 2035.

00:03:37.322 --> 00:03:40.758
Next. "When one celestial body
revolves around another,

00:03:40.825 --> 00:03:41.826
what is it called?"

00:03:41.893 --> 00:03:42.727
I don't know.

00:03:43.294 --> 00:03:44.929
-Revolution.
-Is it getting better?

00:03:44.996 --> 00:03:46.431
Hmm? Getting better?

00:03:46.497 --> 00:03:49.467
Ah, revolution, as in not changing
for the better,

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.169
but in terms of orbiting.

00:03:52.904 --> 00:03:56.541
"The motion of a celestial body spinning
around its own axis is called?"

00:03:56.607 --> 00:03:57.408
Being alive!

00:03:58.376 --> 00:04:00.545
That’s fine. I like that answer,

00:04:00.611 --> 00:04:02.180
but the answer is rotation, okay?

00:04:02.246 --> 00:04:04.549
"In outer space, all stars

00:04:04.615 --> 00:04:05.550
are doing what?"

00:04:06.351 --> 00:04:08.619
-I don't know anymore!
-Hint is the same as before.

00:04:09.153 --> 00:04:10.355
-Being alive!
-Rotation.

00:04:13.391 --> 00:04:15.493
Sorry for interrupting!

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.796
I’ve been practicing photography lately.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.932
Mind being my models for a bit?

00:04:20.998 --> 00:04:23.534
Say cheese!

00:04:24.802 --> 00:04:25.770
There you are.

00:04:25.837 --> 00:04:27.939
About the gas supply, Ms. Landlady…

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.476
-Perfect, you join in too!
-Yeah.

00:04:31.542 --> 00:04:33.611
-What's going on?
-Stand here.

00:04:33.678 --> 00:04:34.512
‎Yeah.

00:04:36.047 --> 00:04:38.483
Okay, say cheese!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.218
Thank you.

00:04:40.284 --> 00:04:41.886
What's this about?

00:04:41.953 --> 00:04:43.688
-You were saying gas supply?
-Yes.

00:04:47.291 --> 00:04:48.426
-Come this way.
-Huh?

00:04:58.536 --> 00:05:01.038
What, you going somewhere?

00:05:01.105 --> 00:05:02.573
-For a bit.
-A bit?

00:05:03.174 --> 00:05:06.310
I’ve studied enough. Thanks for your help.

00:05:07.645 --> 00:05:10.047
You won’t get into high school
at this rate.

00:05:10.114 --> 00:05:11.549
I don’t even know if I’ll go.

00:05:11.616 --> 00:05:13.918
-Are you planning to work?
-I don't know.

00:05:13.985 --> 00:05:15.853
You can’t just not know!

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.522
It’s not my fault.

00:05:17.588 --> 00:05:19.290
I really don’t know, that's why.

00:05:19.357 --> 00:05:20.725
I don’t know anything!

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.832
Well, in a situation like this…

00:05:28.466 --> 00:05:30.935
We can't really blame her, huh?

00:05:31.002 --> 00:05:32.270
We really can't.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.440
That doesn’t make it okay, though.

00:05:35.506 --> 00:05:37.241
If only she comes back soon.

00:05:37.308 --> 00:05:39.076
Her mom, that is.

00:05:39.143 --> 00:05:41.612
Even if she does, she’s a criminal!

00:05:41.679 --> 00:05:43.247
Maybe she was falsely accused.

00:05:43.314 --> 00:05:44.849
You’re way too optimistic.

00:05:44.916 --> 00:05:46.050
Leave it to me.

00:05:46.918 --> 00:05:48.252
In any case, I'm heading out.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.624
T-To where?

00:05:53.691 --> 00:05:55.293
COULD WE MEET?

00:05:55.359 --> 00:05:56.928
JUST THE TWO OF US

00:05:56.994 --> 00:05:58.463
BY TOMOE KUSUNOKI

00:05:58.529 --> 00:06:00.465
This is a huge mission…

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.835
Welcome!

00:06:10.374 --> 00:06:13.544
Which questions
will be on the science test?

00:06:14.378 --> 00:06:18.249
Let me see… That'd be page fif--
As if that's something to be shared!

00:06:20.017 --> 00:06:21.419
Hello!

00:06:22.019 --> 00:06:22.854
Saku!

00:06:23.721 --> 00:06:24.655
He's here.

00:06:31.128 --> 00:06:33.264
Seriously? No way…

00:06:37.635 --> 00:06:40.104
-What's the meaning of this?
-Huh?

00:06:40.171 --> 00:06:41.606
You broke up with him, right?

00:06:41.672 --> 00:06:44.308
We did. I just thought
more hands would help.

00:06:44.909 --> 00:06:46.344
There are plenty of other people…

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.112
-Besides, I like it.
-What?

00:06:48.179 --> 00:06:49.814
The part where he reads manuals.

00:06:50.815 --> 00:06:53.484
-That's a rare breed.
-Right?

00:06:53.551 --> 00:06:55.653
Hey, mind giving me a hand with this?

00:06:56.554 --> 00:06:57.555
Sure!

00:06:59.557 --> 00:07:01.259
It’s been a while.

00:07:01.325 --> 00:07:03.394
Are you sure you don't
need disguises or anything?

00:07:03.461 --> 00:07:06.097
The news isn’t even featuring it anymore.

00:07:07.265 --> 00:07:09.033
What’s the business today?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.202
Welcome.

00:07:13.638 --> 00:07:15.406
Have you decided on your order?

00:07:16.474 --> 00:07:18.976
-Iced coffee, please.
-Very well.

00:07:21.145 --> 00:07:23.281
So, what’s the matter?

00:07:24.515 --> 00:07:27.151
I was surprised by the letter.

00:07:28.252 --> 00:07:31.255
We never really had
a proper conversation before.

00:07:31.322 --> 00:07:33.991
I thought it might’ve been meant
for Hotaru by mistake.

00:07:35.927 --> 00:07:36.928
These…

00:07:37.528 --> 00:07:40.031
I want you to give these to Hotaru.

00:07:40.097 --> 00:07:41.098
These, you mean?

00:07:41.899 --> 00:07:43.334
She’ll understand once she sees it.

00:07:45.136 --> 00:07:47.505
Did you really do it?

00:07:50.775 --> 00:07:52.009
That's why I ran away.

00:07:52.577 --> 00:07:54.412
I see. Okay…

00:07:54.979 --> 00:07:56.047
Got it.

00:07:56.914 --> 00:07:58.549
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:58.616 --> 00:08:02.553
Cream soda and iced coffee.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.155
Please enjoy.

00:08:05.256 --> 00:08:07.625
Probably not the best time for this order.

00:08:13.097 --> 00:08:14.565
I came here today

00:08:14.632 --> 00:08:17.134
to bring you back with me.

00:08:23.574 --> 00:08:25.610
At first, I thought you two
would be living together.

00:08:25.676 --> 00:08:27.345
I was like, "Wow, that escalated fast."

00:08:27.411 --> 00:08:29.013
Are you curious?

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.549
Nah, I’m the type

00:08:31.616 --> 00:08:34.018
who can go back to being friends
with an ex.

00:08:34.085 --> 00:08:35.319
I think Saku is too.

00:08:35.386 --> 00:08:37.655
I usually just cut off contact.

00:08:38.422 --> 00:08:41.492
-Makes sense. No surprise there.
-What do you mean?

00:08:41.559 --> 00:08:42.760
-Go a little right.
-Right?

00:08:42.827 --> 00:08:45.296
Ah, not that side! People normally go
the opposite way.

00:08:45.363 --> 00:08:47.865
Your normal and my normal are different!

00:08:47.932 --> 00:08:50.267
When people say right or left
in this situation,

00:08:50.334 --> 00:08:52.970
wouldn't the other party assume
it's their right or left?

00:08:53.037 --> 00:08:55.072
Then you should've just said so.

00:08:55.139 --> 00:08:56.774
Yeah, yeah. My bad.

00:08:56.841 --> 00:08:57.975
What a grumpy old man.

00:08:58.576 --> 00:09:00.678
-Did you just call me old?
-I'm 33 years old.

00:09:01.379 --> 00:09:02.680
-You're young.
-See?

00:09:02.747 --> 00:09:05.716
That proves you’re the old man.

00:09:05.783 --> 00:09:07.718
Could you hurry up, please?

00:09:07.785 --> 00:09:08.986
Could you hurry?

00:09:09.053 --> 00:09:10.287
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:11.522 --> 00:09:12.523
What's this?

00:09:13.691 --> 00:09:14.992
Buttercream sandwich I reserved.

00:09:15.059 --> 00:09:16.260
You really love it, huh?

00:09:16.327 --> 00:09:18.829
Don’t you dare eat them!
I waited three months for it!

00:09:18.896 --> 00:09:19.964
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:21.632 --> 00:09:23.968
Alright, first step…

00:09:24.035 --> 00:09:25.369
Before that,

00:09:25.936 --> 00:09:27.638
aren’t you a little hungry?

00:09:30.174 --> 00:09:31.609
You don't want anything to eat?

00:09:31.676 --> 00:09:33.077
What about a sandwich?

00:09:34.512 --> 00:09:36.047
Being on the run costs money too.

00:09:36.113 --> 00:09:37.715
Oh, right.

00:09:37.782 --> 00:09:40.351
All the money is with Hotaru.

00:09:40.418 --> 00:09:41.452
Yes.

00:09:41.519 --> 00:09:42.853
So, it was for Hotaru after all?

00:09:44.055 --> 00:09:45.923
You embezzled for Hotaru's sake?

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:47.425
No,

00:09:48.259 --> 00:09:49.460
that's not it.

00:09:51.462 --> 00:09:52.997
I did it for myself.

00:09:55.966 --> 00:09:59.236
-Koinobori.
-What's wrong?

00:09:59.303 --> 00:10:01.806
-I don’t get this part.
-Which part?

00:10:01.872 --> 00:10:04.742
I'm kinda craving fries.

00:10:05.309 --> 00:10:07.344
-Look!
-No way!

00:10:07.411 --> 00:10:09.947
A coupon where you can get fries for free!

00:10:10.014 --> 00:10:12.216
-Awesome!
-I'm so hungry!

00:10:12.283 --> 00:10:13.150
-Let's go now.
-I'm excited!

00:10:13.217 --> 00:10:14.452
-Already?
-Yeah, let's go.

00:10:14.518 --> 00:10:15.586
Nacchi, you too!

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.455
Huh?

00:10:17.521 --> 00:10:19.156
We're going to get free fries.

00:10:20.624 --> 00:10:21.926
I'll pass.

00:10:21.992 --> 00:10:23.494
Why don't you join them?

00:10:23.561 --> 00:10:25.096
Studying is more important.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.765
Are you going to high school?

00:10:27.832 --> 00:10:29.734
-Yeah.
-And after that?

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.368
What do you mean?

00:10:31.435 --> 00:10:33.537
Let's go, Hotaru!

00:10:37.608 --> 00:10:39.910
I wonder why Nacchi
suddenly started studying.

00:10:39.977 --> 00:10:42.213
Maybe she wants to be rich?

00:10:42.279 --> 00:10:44.415
Wait. Is Nacchi’s family poor?

00:10:44.482 --> 00:10:45.416
Not sure.

00:10:47.084 --> 00:10:48.486
What's her last name?

00:10:49.153 --> 00:10:50.287
I don't know.

00:10:50.955 --> 00:10:52.623
What school does she go to?

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:53.891
No idea about that too.

00:10:53.958 --> 00:10:54.859
What, you curious?

00:10:54.925 --> 00:10:57.194
I just realized I don’t actually
know anything about her.

00:10:59.597 --> 00:11:00.464
Delicious!

00:11:01.031 --> 00:11:02.233
This is absolute bliss.

00:11:02.299 --> 00:11:04.235
You like it that much?

00:11:04.301 --> 00:11:06.370
He used to take me to pizza places a lot.

00:11:07.638 --> 00:11:09.206
Ah, that place in Meguro?

00:11:10.241 --> 00:11:12.743
We can't go there anymore though.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:13.944
What? Why?

00:11:15.079 --> 00:11:17.148
I went there recently with a friend,

00:11:17.214 --> 00:11:18.649
who's another gay guy.

00:11:19.416 --> 00:11:21.719
We were drinking wine

00:11:21.786 --> 00:11:23.154
and got carried away.

00:11:23.721 --> 00:11:26.757
I think everyone overheard us
talking about our love lives.

00:11:27.691 --> 00:11:31.028
I did notice people glancing at us,

00:11:31.095 --> 00:11:32.997
but then, this guy at the next table goes,

00:11:33.063 --> 00:11:36.000
"What are gays doing here?"

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:37.601
What the heck?

00:11:37.668 --> 00:11:40.437
Maybe he thought we only hung out
in the gay district or something?

00:11:41.005 --> 00:11:44.675
Anyway, everyone else was staring too,

00:11:44.742 --> 00:11:47.311
and I didn’t want to cause
any more trouble, so we left.

00:11:48.546 --> 00:11:51.248
After that, we couldn’t go back there.

00:11:51.816 --> 00:11:52.950
You don’t get stuff like that?

00:11:53.517 --> 00:11:56.320
Not so blatant lately,

00:11:56.921 --> 00:11:59.089
but yeah, that happened a lot
back in the day.

00:11:59.156 --> 00:12:02.259
"Gay people are contagious!" and such.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.863
Feels like, from way back then until now,

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.965
people have just been looking down on us.

00:12:08.032 --> 00:12:11.402
I realized I was being looked down on.

00:12:11.468 --> 00:12:12.469
By who?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.772
Society as a whole, I guess?

00:12:14.839 --> 00:12:15.973
That's a grand picture.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.142
Back when I was job hunting,

00:12:18.209 --> 00:12:20.044
it was the employment ice age.

00:12:20.711 --> 00:12:23.380
I really, truly had no job prospects.

00:12:23.447 --> 00:12:25.182
No matter how big the company was,

00:12:25.249 --> 00:12:27.651
it seemed like they were only hiring
two or three people

00:12:27.718 --> 00:12:29.019
as full-time employees.

00:12:29.086 --> 00:12:30.187
I mean,

00:12:30.254 --> 00:12:32.289
who could even pass?
It just felt impossible.

00:12:32.356 --> 00:12:34.425
Those were rough times.

00:12:34.491 --> 00:12:35.793
I ended up as a contract staff

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.395
doing accounting.

00:12:38.462 --> 00:12:41.532
-The same company the entire time?
-Yes.

00:12:42.199 --> 00:12:43.634
You must be really competent.

00:12:43.701 --> 00:12:46.737
No, actually, I was pretty much useless.

00:12:47.371 --> 00:12:49.173
The reason my contract wasn't terminated

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.575
was because I wasn’t "troublesome".

00:12:52.309 --> 00:12:53.477
What do you mean?

00:12:53.544 --> 00:12:57.281
You know how women who oppose
or have a strong sense of justice

00:12:57.348 --> 00:12:58.916
are often called "troublesome"?

00:12:58.983 --> 00:13:01.852
"This contract clause is weird."

00:13:01.919 --> 00:13:04.188
"Can we do something about the pay?"

00:13:04.255 --> 00:13:05.823
That’s considered "troublesome".

00:13:06.724 --> 00:13:10.694
I was just spacing out,
not thinking about anything.

00:13:11.595 --> 00:13:13.430
After Hotaru was born,

00:13:13.497 --> 00:13:15.032
I had even less time to think.

00:13:15.599 --> 00:13:17.434
I had to buy the discounted tomatoes,

00:13:17.501 --> 00:13:20.371
check when my points expire, etc.

00:13:20.437 --> 00:13:21.972
My head was full of stuff like that.

00:13:22.806 --> 00:13:25.843
With the company, I’d just say,
"Okay, okay, got it."

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:28.379
That wasn’t "troublesome" in their books.

00:13:29.046 --> 00:13:31.849
That’s probably why
my contract got renewed.

00:13:32.416 --> 00:13:34.151
Everyone else who joined at the same time,

00:13:34.218 --> 00:13:37.621
seniors, juniors, and peers alike,
if they were "troublesome",

00:13:37.688 --> 00:13:39.423
they either left or got replaced.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:40.958
-Welcome.
-A table for one.

00:13:41.025 --> 00:13:42.192
Have a seat over there.

00:13:42.259 --> 00:13:43.193
Thank you.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.595
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

00:13:44.662 --> 00:13:48.699
It’s a bit cold, so could you
turn up the heat?

00:13:48.766 --> 00:13:50.301
Certainly.

00:13:52.736 --> 00:13:54.438
She might think I'm "troublesome".

00:13:55.372 --> 00:13:58.709
I was cold too, so I’m glad
you said something.

00:13:58.776 --> 00:13:59.777
Thanks.

00:14:01.612 --> 00:14:03.380
Sorry, I just kind of

00:14:03.447 --> 00:14:05.149
let it all out.

00:14:05.916 --> 00:14:06.984
You’d been holding it in?

00:14:09.119 --> 00:14:11.622
-Welcome.
-Thank you.

00:14:13.023 --> 00:14:16.093
Do you have anything with a bit of a kick?

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.294
I want to be pumped.

00:14:17.795 --> 00:14:19.897
So… Where was I again?

00:14:19.964 --> 00:14:22.032
Why did you do it?

00:14:26.804 --> 00:14:28.772
A year ago,

00:14:28.839 --> 00:14:31.675
a young man joined as a contract staff,

00:14:31.742 --> 00:14:34.611
and he became a full-time employee.

00:14:34.678 --> 00:14:39.583
Something neither the other women
nor I could achieve, even after decades.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.485
And he did it in just one year.

00:14:41.552 --> 00:14:42.486
Why was that?

00:14:43.387 --> 00:14:44.688
Exactly!

00:14:44.755 --> 00:14:46.490
Why, right?

00:14:47.391 --> 00:14:50.594
I couldn’t keep from being
"troublesome" any longer,

00:14:50.661 --> 00:14:51.762
so I asked for the reason.

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.366
And that was "15 minutes".

00:14:55.432 --> 00:14:56.600
Huh?

00:14:57.701 --> 00:14:59.203
That person

00:14:59.269 --> 00:15:02.339
came in 15 minutes earlier
than me every morning

00:15:02.406 --> 00:15:04.408
and left 15 minutes later than me.

00:15:05.642 --> 00:15:07.344
His dedication was evaluated.

00:15:07.945 --> 00:15:10.614
-What?
-I was like, "What the hell?"

00:15:12.016 --> 00:15:15.452
And if "15 minutes"…

00:15:15.519 --> 00:15:18.188
If that was truly the reason…

00:15:18.255 --> 00:15:20.424
My extra 15 minutes in the morning was for

00:15:20.491 --> 00:15:23.394
those idiots who said things like,
"Looking pretty is part of your job,"

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.928
so I had to put on foundation.

00:15:24.995 --> 00:15:26.663
The 15 minutes I left early…

00:15:27.731 --> 00:15:29.299
were for Hotaru.

00:15:29.366 --> 00:15:31.135
I had to make her meals.

00:15:32.136 --> 00:15:34.238
So, the young man

00:15:34.304 --> 00:15:36.140
was wearing makeup?

00:15:36.206 --> 00:15:38.208
Was he told to look pretty?

00:15:39.943 --> 00:15:41.545
Did he have kids?

00:15:41.612 --> 00:15:42.813
Did he have to do housework?

00:15:44.048 --> 00:15:45.215
I figured.

00:15:45.282 --> 00:15:48.585
Most men probably wouldn’t understand
what those 15 minutes mean.

00:15:48.652 --> 00:15:50.220
That’s when I realized…

00:15:51.555 --> 00:15:54.291
I’d been looked down on
just because I’m a woman, all along.

00:15:55.325 --> 00:15:57.127
Once I got bothered about one matter,

00:15:57.194 --> 00:15:58.896
I started noticing everything.

00:15:58.962 --> 00:16:02.332
When I looked into it using my decades
of accounting experience,

00:16:02.399 --> 00:16:04.968
there was a wage gap
between men and women.

00:16:05.035 --> 00:16:07.137
Five hundred and four yen per hour.

00:16:07.204 --> 00:16:08.906
As for why there was a difference,

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:11.542
there was no proper reason for it.

00:16:13.043 --> 00:16:17.014
Contract roles were mostly filled
by women to begin with.

00:16:17.081 --> 00:16:18.916
Even women who had been
full-time employees

00:16:18.982 --> 00:16:21.318
and left due to marriage or pregnancy

00:16:21.385 --> 00:16:24.321
couldn’t return as full-timers,
and they ended up working temp jobs.

00:16:24.888 --> 00:16:25.923
At the end of the day,

00:16:26.657 --> 00:16:30.160
if you have kids,
your schedule couldn’t be flexible,

00:16:30.227 --> 00:16:32.096
and that was frowned upon too.

00:16:32.796 --> 00:16:34.331
But none of this was our fault.

00:16:35.432 --> 00:16:37.868
So, I tried calculating it.

00:16:38.702 --> 00:16:41.371
The money I didn’t get
because I was a contract staff.

00:16:41.438 --> 00:16:44.141
The money I didn’t get
because I was a woman.

00:16:44.808 --> 00:16:45.876
My money…

00:16:46.643 --> 00:16:47.778
all added up to…

00:16:48.445 --> 00:16:51.415
32,261,570 yen.

00:16:52.015 --> 00:16:54.051
Did you embezzle that amount?

00:16:54.118 --> 00:16:55.252
No.

00:16:55.319 --> 00:16:57.654
Well, yes…

00:16:57.721 --> 00:17:00.657
But that’s not why I calculated it.

00:17:01.158 --> 00:17:03.427
I just thought,
"Wow, that’s how much it comes to."

00:17:03.494 --> 00:17:05.629
But I couldn’t do anything about it.

00:17:06.196 --> 00:17:07.030
Then why?

00:17:07.097 --> 00:17:08.966
The career sheet.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.335
-Hotaru's?
-Yes.

00:17:13.203 --> 00:17:15.506
When she brought it home,

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.475
she asked, "Can I go to high school?

00:17:18.542 --> 00:17:21.178
Is there a cheap one?"

00:17:22.713 --> 00:17:23.680
I assured her

00:17:24.715 --> 00:17:27.885
that for now, we don't have to pay
tuition fees, and there are subsidies,

00:17:27.951 --> 00:17:29.653
so she doesn't have to worry.

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:31.321
I just laughed it off.

00:17:32.256 --> 00:17:33.257
But somehow…

00:17:33.991 --> 00:17:35.159
it stings.

00:17:37.094 --> 00:17:38.595
What she wanted to do,

00:17:38.662 --> 00:17:40.197
what she liked,

00:17:40.264 --> 00:17:41.732
which high school she wanted to go to…

00:17:42.332 --> 00:17:43.467
More than those things,

00:17:44.268 --> 00:17:46.470
seeing Hotaru worry about money instead

00:17:47.538 --> 00:17:48.672
made me feel awful.

00:17:50.107 --> 00:17:50.941
Then, bam!

00:17:51.508 --> 00:17:53.210
Suddenly, the number

00:17:53.277 --> 00:17:56.446
32,261,570

00:17:58.348 --> 00:17:59.616
popped into my head.

00:18:01.118 --> 00:18:02.152
And…

00:18:03.587 --> 00:18:05.022
I just kinda got furious.

00:18:07.157 --> 00:18:08.358
At first,

00:18:08.926 --> 00:18:11.728
I took the 170 yen sitting
on my boss’s desk

00:18:11.795 --> 00:18:13.597
on a whim.

00:18:15.232 --> 00:18:16.233
I didn't get caught.

00:18:17.901 --> 00:18:18.969
After that,

00:18:19.036 --> 00:18:20.170
I couldn’t go back.

00:18:21.004 --> 00:18:22.606
Hundred and seventy yen

00:18:22.673 --> 00:18:25.609
or 32,261,570 yen… It’s all the same!

00:18:25.676 --> 00:18:28.612
No, it's not.

00:18:28.679 --> 00:18:30.113
I wanted to be

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:34.051
the kind of mother who never made
her child worry about money.

00:18:34.117 --> 00:18:35.852
I wanted to.

00:18:35.919 --> 00:18:36.887
I really did.

00:18:38.322 --> 00:18:39.623
That was why I stole…

00:18:40.724 --> 00:18:41.858
the money.

00:18:43.727 --> 00:18:46.029
I did it for myself.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:49.132
-When?
-Some time in the future.

00:18:49.199 --> 00:18:50.734
-Future, huh?
-Oh, that's Nacchi.

00:18:51.535 --> 00:18:53.370
What? You're right.

00:19:28.805 --> 00:19:30.607
"Amazingly sharp"?

00:19:30.674 --> 00:19:31.842
RAZOR FOR 199 YEN

00:19:31.908 --> 00:19:34.711
No, that’s the wrong one!
That goes over here, right?

00:19:34.778 --> 00:19:35.979
Okay.

00:19:36.046 --> 00:19:37.748
Then, this screw goes here?

00:19:37.814 --> 00:19:40.250
-No, both of you are wrong!
-We're both wrong?

00:19:40.317 --> 00:19:42.819
How can you both look at the same diagram
and still be lost?

00:19:42.886 --> 00:19:44.254
Are you guys seeing different things?

00:19:44.321 --> 00:19:45.689
Forget it. Hand it over! Ow!

00:19:48.592 --> 00:19:51.228
Guess that’s the consequence
of not trying to talk it out.

00:19:51.295 --> 00:19:52.829
You yanked it too hard.

00:19:52.896 --> 00:19:55.499
It’s because you can’t even read
the instructions properly.

00:19:55.565 --> 00:19:56.400
It hurts…

00:19:57.768 --> 00:19:58.769
Here you go.

00:19:59.469 --> 00:20:00.437
Thanks.

00:20:02.439 --> 00:20:03.640
What is it this time?

00:20:03.707 --> 00:20:06.410
-My ring is missing.
-What ring?

00:20:06.476 --> 00:20:07.577
See?

00:20:08.145 --> 00:20:09.846
-Oh, the dummy one.
-Right!

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:14.651
It's not here…

00:20:14.718 --> 00:20:15.886
Is it in this room?

00:20:16.586 --> 00:20:18.822
-Probably.
-There’s always that

00:20:18.889 --> 00:20:21.558
one person who loses things
in the weirdest ways, no?

00:20:22.326 --> 00:20:24.861
Do you usually pretend you're married?

00:20:24.928 --> 00:20:25.996
Yes.

00:20:26.063 --> 00:20:28.065
Well, especially at work.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:31.902
It’s convenient.

00:20:31.968 --> 00:20:34.071
It’s an easy sign.

00:20:34.137 --> 00:20:36.907
People don’t directly ask,
"Do you have a girlfriend?"

00:20:36.973 --> 00:20:39.376
or "Do you plan to get married?"

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:41.778
It's basically
a little transformation tool.

00:20:42.746 --> 00:20:46.283
-What do you mean?
-You know, like a Rider Belt.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.185
Or a Magic Compact.

00:20:49.486 --> 00:20:51.788
An item that lets you be a normal person.

00:20:52.723 --> 00:20:54.725
It makes you feel like
you fit in with society.

00:20:55.459 --> 00:20:57.761
Maybe that’s why you never really fit in?

00:20:58.662 --> 00:21:00.964
-What?
-Because you hide and lie about it,

00:21:01.031 --> 00:21:02.366
so nothing ever changes.

00:21:03.333 --> 00:21:06.970
It’s not like it’s something
we need to publicize.

00:21:07.037 --> 00:21:09.573
If all of us just said we're gay
when asked,

00:21:09.639 --> 00:21:12.542
maybe the world would change,
is what I think sometimes.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.246
To begin with, maybe people don’t know
we’re just everywhere.

00:21:16.313 --> 00:21:18.248
That's why prejudice exists, I think.

00:21:18.315 --> 00:21:21.184
Because we're often hurt by it
to begin with,

00:21:22.419 --> 00:21:23.553
so people don’t say anything.

00:21:27.724 --> 00:21:28.759
Not here!

00:21:29.826 --> 00:21:30.994
The ring is gone.

00:21:31.561 --> 00:21:33.230
It's a cheap one anyway. No issues.

00:21:33.296 --> 00:21:35.132
Thank you.

00:21:35.198 --> 00:21:36.733
Let's assemble the bed!

00:21:37.234 --> 00:21:39.970
Just from being a woman myself,

00:21:40.036 --> 00:21:42.072
I’ve had those "Excuse me?" moments too.

00:21:42.139 --> 00:21:43.006
Right.

00:21:43.073 --> 00:21:46.910
Back in my day, it was the opposite
of your experience, Tomoe.

00:21:46.977 --> 00:21:49.513
I just happened to be born at a good time.

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.381
The economy was booming.

00:21:51.915 --> 00:21:54.117
I graduated from a commercial high school

00:21:54.184 --> 00:21:56.686
and landed a job at a company
in those huge office buildings.

00:21:56.753 --> 00:21:59.890
I was so thrilled. I felt like I was going
to be those stylish office ladies.

00:21:59.956 --> 00:22:02.192
That's nice. Full of sparkle.

00:22:02.259 --> 00:22:05.662
But then, there were those
training sessions,

00:22:05.729 --> 00:22:08.965
and we were separated by gender.

00:22:09.032 --> 00:22:10.000
Yeah.

00:22:10.066 --> 00:22:13.603
Men got manuals and classroom learning.

00:22:14.971 --> 00:22:18.074
And guess what the women had to do?

00:22:19.009 --> 00:22:21.678
-What was it?
-On everyone's mugs,

00:22:21.745 --> 00:22:24.047
we had to write names. By hand.
One by one.

00:22:24.748 --> 00:22:25.782
Huh, what?

00:22:25.849 --> 00:22:28.118
All the mugs were the same white ones.

00:22:29.286 --> 00:22:34.224
So, "Aoki", "Katsumata",
"Tanaka", "Watanabe",

00:22:34.291 --> 00:22:35.492
and so on…

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:38.061
That makes no sense at all.

00:22:38.128 --> 00:22:39.463
I know, right?

00:22:39.529 --> 00:22:41.598
They told us, "This is your first task,

00:22:41.665 --> 00:22:43.300
so give it your all."

00:22:43.867 --> 00:22:44.935
Ridiculous.

00:22:45.001 --> 00:22:48.205
"If young girls write the names

00:22:48.271 --> 00:22:50.373
and even remember them too,

00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:53.076
it’d motivate the male employees,"

00:22:53.143 --> 00:22:54.311
was what the boss said.

00:22:55.111 --> 00:22:56.079
Disgusting.

00:22:56.146 --> 00:22:58.515
Even after that first task,

00:22:58.582 --> 00:23:00.650
they said women are just more thoughtful

00:23:00.717 --> 00:23:02.118
and kept dumping chores on us.

00:23:02.185 --> 00:23:04.221
Being thoughtful or not
depends on the person.

00:23:04.287 --> 00:23:05.288
Exactly.

00:23:06.089 --> 00:23:07.958
Oh, did you ever get that?

00:23:08.024 --> 00:23:10.527
Like, "We’d like
a woman’s perspective on this."

00:23:10.594 --> 00:23:12.095
That depends on the person too, no?

00:23:12.162 --> 00:23:13.430
Exactly!

00:23:14.297 --> 00:23:17.033
Guess things haven’t changed much
since my time.

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:18.935
-Right?
-But…

00:23:20.303 --> 00:23:23.807
I can't say I can fully empathize
with what you've been through.

00:23:29.846 --> 00:23:31.481
Thank you for waiting.

00:23:32.048 --> 00:23:32.916
That's huge!

00:23:32.983 --> 00:23:34.384
Please enjoy.

00:23:39.523 --> 00:23:40.557
Let's do this!

00:23:46.463 --> 00:23:48.798
I quit my job after three months.

00:23:49.699 --> 00:23:52.536
It wasn’t the office life I imagined.

00:23:53.436 --> 00:23:55.038
I wanted to do more meaningful work

00:23:55.105 --> 00:23:57.440
and be recognized and praised for it.

00:23:57.507 --> 00:23:59.209
I wanted to do stuff like that,

00:23:59.276 --> 00:24:00.310
but I couldn't.

00:24:00.377 --> 00:24:01.811
What did you do after quitting?

00:24:01.878 --> 00:24:03.813
My parents ran an apartment building.

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:05.882
I helped out there a bit

00:24:05.949 --> 00:24:07.584
and spent my time doing what I liked.

00:24:07.651 --> 00:24:08.785
I see.

00:24:08.852 --> 00:24:11.655
I had that feeling I had to make
something out of myself,

00:24:12.155 --> 00:24:14.190
so I tried doing all sorts of things.

00:24:14.958 --> 00:24:17.093
But in the end, I didn’t become anything.

00:24:17.827 --> 00:24:20.196
No marriage. No kids.

00:24:21.431 --> 00:24:23.633
You see, my family
had a decent amount of money,

00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:25.135
so I could live like that.

00:24:26.069 --> 00:24:28.672
I never really held a grudge
against that company

00:24:28.738 --> 00:24:29.573
or acted dangerously…

00:24:31.341 --> 00:24:34.110
or get involved in any crimes. Nothing.

00:24:35.312 --> 00:24:37.247
I lived a quiet life.

00:24:37.314 --> 00:24:40.684
That's why I could never say,
"I totally get you."

00:24:41.384 --> 00:24:43.420
And you probably wouldn’t
want to hear it from me.

00:24:45.322 --> 00:24:47.090
And one more thing.

00:24:47.157 --> 00:24:50.527
I felt I had to say this
ever since I got the letter.

00:24:51.161 --> 00:24:53.229
-What is it?
-It's about Hotaru.

00:24:55.098 --> 00:24:58.101
If I were in your shoes,
I’d never leave her behind.

00:24:58.735 --> 00:25:00.904
Even if I had to run,
I’d take her with me.

00:25:02.205 --> 00:25:03.974
I think she’s a capable child.

00:25:04.774 --> 00:25:06.977
She seems perfectly fine.

00:25:07.544 --> 00:25:08.378
But

00:25:09.679 --> 00:25:13.016
betrayal by the people they trust most…

00:25:13.083 --> 00:25:14.818
You can’t let a child experience that.

00:25:15.452 --> 00:25:17.454
Even if it means leaving money
behind or not.

00:25:19.089 --> 00:25:20.090
I understand.

00:25:20.156 --> 00:25:22.392
No, you don't. That's why
you don't come back, right?

00:25:22.926 --> 00:25:24.394
Why do you keep running?

00:25:53.790 --> 00:25:58.461
This person from the apartment
has been kind to Hotaru,

00:25:58.528 --> 00:26:00.563
and this is her teacher.

00:26:00.630 --> 00:26:02.999
He's also going to be living with us.

00:26:14.611 --> 00:26:16.079
Can't you return?

00:26:19.115 --> 00:26:22.118
There’s something I absolutely have to do.

00:26:22.185 --> 00:26:24.087
Really?

00:26:24.154 --> 00:26:25.355
I…

00:26:25.989 --> 00:26:29.459
In order to become a proper mom
to Hotaru again,

00:26:30.694 --> 00:26:32.262
there's something I must do.

00:26:33.029 --> 00:26:33.930
Hotaru…

00:26:34.564 --> 00:26:37.701
When she receives these keychains,
she’ll understand.

00:26:39.869 --> 00:26:41.104
I need more time…

00:26:42.138 --> 00:26:43.039
Please.

00:26:43.106 --> 00:26:46.476
Does it have anything to do
with what you have to do?

00:26:46.543 --> 00:26:47.877
Just a little longer.

00:26:48.978 --> 00:26:49.813
I'm begging you.

00:26:49.879 --> 00:26:52.682
Really? Just a little more?

00:26:54.217 --> 00:26:55.985
-Yes.
-You'd better keep your promise.

00:26:56.886 --> 00:27:00.390
Or I’ll have the police come.

00:27:02.492 --> 00:27:03.960
P-Police?

00:27:04.027 --> 00:27:07.163
They came to the apartment to ask about
things, just in case something happens.

00:27:11.134 --> 00:27:12.068
I'll keep my promise.

00:27:15.839 --> 00:27:17.874
In the meantime, I’ll take care of Hotaru.

00:27:20.143 --> 00:27:21.344
Am I your accomplice now?

00:27:23.179 --> 00:27:24.614
Maybe you are.

00:27:24.681 --> 00:27:26.583
This is starting to get exciting.

00:27:29.953 --> 00:27:30.920
Um…

00:27:31.621 --> 00:27:34.591
I’ve been wondering
about that for a while.

00:27:35.725 --> 00:27:36.793
That.

00:27:43.066 --> 00:27:43.933
Is she calling us?

00:27:44.834 --> 00:27:46.336
Seems like it.

00:27:52.509 --> 00:27:55.278
-Too late for that now.
-Yeah, I know.

00:27:55.345 --> 00:27:56.479
Did you follow me?

00:27:59.048 --> 00:28:00.316
You want to go to this high school?

00:28:00.383 --> 00:28:02.051
Well, it’s on my list, I guess.

00:28:02.118 --> 00:28:05.088
You really think about your future, huh?

00:28:05.155 --> 00:28:06.689
My future…

00:28:07.557 --> 00:28:09.359
I don’t really know about that, but…

00:28:11.594 --> 00:28:14.664
Look! The people walking over there,

00:28:14.731 --> 00:28:16.332
the people running over there,

00:28:16.399 --> 00:28:18.234
and the people throwing balls over there…

00:28:18.301 --> 00:28:20.136
Everyone’s eyebrows are thin, no?

00:28:20.904 --> 00:28:23.740
-Huh, eyebrows?
-I want to shave mine.

00:28:24.474 --> 00:28:25.542
What's stopping you?

00:28:25.608 --> 00:28:27.710
Well, my middle school doesn't allow it.

00:28:27.777 --> 00:28:29.879
Then, I heard a rumor.

00:28:29.946 --> 00:28:31.614
High-score schools

00:28:31.681 --> 00:28:33.950
and smart companies
let you shave your eyebrows.

00:28:34.017 --> 00:28:36.886
Their rules are loose.
You're free to do what you want.

00:28:37.854 --> 00:28:38.688
That’s why you study?

00:28:39.255 --> 00:28:42.559
I just want to shave my eyebrows freely
without getting into trouble for it.

00:28:42.625 --> 00:28:43.893
That’s the career path I chose.

00:28:46.296 --> 00:28:48.398
-Hey!
-Sorry.

00:28:49.132 --> 00:28:50.934
Is that why you were staring
at that razor?

00:28:51.901 --> 00:28:53.503
You saw that?

00:28:53.570 --> 00:28:55.705
If I study little by little,

00:28:55.772 --> 00:28:57.807
maybe I can get thin eyebrows.

00:28:57.874 --> 00:28:59.943
By the time my eyebrows are thin,

00:29:00.009 --> 00:29:02.478
my parents and money and stuff
will get better,

00:29:02.545 --> 00:29:05.148
and you, Bayashiko, and Myoga,
will be doing great too.

00:29:05.215 --> 00:29:08.618
It’d be great if we could all sing,
dance, and have a party.

00:29:08.685 --> 00:29:10.086
Wouldn't that be nice?

00:29:10.153 --> 00:29:11.487
So…

00:29:12.522 --> 00:29:14.290
I’m going to study hard for my tests.

00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:18.328
Yay!

00:29:18.394 --> 00:29:20.129
We're finally done!

00:29:20.196 --> 00:29:21.397
Shall we carry it?

00:29:21.965 --> 00:29:23.199
In one, two…

00:29:25.401 --> 00:29:27.871
How long has it been
since you slept in a bed?

00:29:27.937 --> 00:29:30.106
About six months.

00:29:30.173 --> 00:29:32.442
-Aren't you excited?
-You can say that again!

00:29:34.477 --> 00:29:36.880
Nice and done.

00:29:36.946 --> 00:29:38.014
Okay!

00:29:38.715 --> 00:29:39.716
Good.

00:29:42.018 --> 00:29:42.852
What's the matter?

00:29:43.586 --> 00:29:44.888
Something fell.

00:29:45.755 --> 00:29:46.956
From where?

00:29:48.992 --> 00:29:51.461
No idea.

00:29:51.527 --> 00:29:54.497
Maybe a spare?

00:29:54.564 --> 00:29:56.432
Those are in the bags.

00:29:56.499 --> 00:29:58.034
Uh, whatever.

00:29:58.101 --> 00:30:00.803
-Won’t it get shaky later?
-Just forget it.

00:30:00.870 --> 00:30:02.105
I’m tired.

00:30:05.375 --> 00:30:07.977
Isn’t it a perfect substitute
for you-know-what?

00:30:09.245 --> 00:30:11.281
-For what?
-Your left ring finger.

00:30:20.423 --> 00:30:22.358
Doesn't it look awkward?

00:30:22.425 --> 00:30:24.527
Oh, no. An avant-garde design, I’d say.

00:30:24.594 --> 00:30:26.162
You think so?

00:30:26.229 --> 00:30:28.831
You know what? I'll buy myself a ring,
like a normal person.

00:30:28.898 --> 00:30:29.999
Isn’t that a waste?

00:30:30.566 --> 00:30:33.336
Years from now, you won’t need it, right?

00:30:33.403 --> 00:30:34.771
The dummy ring.

00:30:36.639 --> 00:30:38.041
We'll be in that kind of era?

00:30:38.107 --> 00:30:40.043
Will it come that fast?

00:30:41.177 --> 00:30:42.211
I don't know.

00:30:42.278 --> 00:30:43.913
It’ll come one day.

00:30:44.547 --> 00:30:45.415
I just know it.

00:30:51.020 --> 00:30:52.121
I hope you're right.

00:30:59.195 --> 00:31:03.132
Sorry for making you share a jumbo parfait
with a complete stranger.

00:31:03.199 --> 00:31:05.702
It’s my first time eating one this big.

00:31:05.768 --> 00:31:08.838
Same here. It’s amazing.

00:31:08.905 --> 00:31:10.340
-It's a first for me too.
-What?

00:31:10.406 --> 00:31:13.176
I just wanted to psych myself up,
so I ordered it.

00:31:13.242 --> 00:31:15.378
But there’s no way I could eat this alone.

00:31:18.681 --> 00:31:20.717
Oh, I'm so sorry!

00:31:20.783 --> 00:31:23.086
Sorry!

00:31:23.152 --> 00:31:25.722
-Oh, dear me…
-Don't worry about it.

00:31:27.690 --> 00:31:29.425
Psyching yourself up
for apartment hunting?

00:31:30.693 --> 00:31:32.028
Sorry, I didn't mean to see it.

00:31:32.095 --> 00:31:35.098
I’m thinking of buying a condo.

00:31:35.164 --> 00:31:38.101
So, I’m working hard,

00:31:38.167 --> 00:31:39.802
trying my best to save up.

00:31:40.903 --> 00:31:42.205
That's impressive.

00:31:42.271 --> 00:31:44.307
Yes, very respectable.

00:31:44.374 --> 00:31:47.210
Today, I was checking out
some condos I’m interested in

00:31:47.276 --> 00:31:48.277
while walking around.

00:31:48.344 --> 00:31:49.946
I see.

00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:52.215
Huh?

00:31:52.281 --> 00:31:54.350
-Isn't this wrong?
-Huh?

00:31:54.417 --> 00:31:57.253
"Nakano Station, 15 hours away on foot."

00:31:57.320 --> 00:31:58.821
They meant minutes, not hours, right?

00:31:58.888 --> 00:31:59.922
You're right!

00:31:59.989 --> 00:32:01.257
Fifteen hours?

00:32:01.324 --> 00:32:04.193
I was actually kind of interested
in this place.

00:32:04.260 --> 00:32:07.463
Well, even if it were true,
it’s not impossible to get there, right?

00:32:07.530 --> 00:32:09.165
-Just have to walk.
-Yeah.

00:32:09.232 --> 00:32:10.199
If you keep walking.

00:32:11.768 --> 00:32:14.237
Assuming you could keep walking, though.

00:32:14.737 --> 00:32:16.406
Thank you!

00:32:22.211 --> 00:32:24.280
I’m heading home after tossing this.

00:32:28.818 --> 00:32:30.553
A little something for you.

00:32:30.620 --> 00:32:31.554
Really?

00:32:31.621 --> 00:32:33.256
Just my way of saying thanks for today.

00:32:33.956 --> 00:32:34.957
I appreciate it.

00:32:35.625 --> 00:32:38.428
There’s a pizza place near that shop.

00:32:39.228 --> 00:32:42.265
It had a pretty long line,
so it might even be better than Meguro's.

00:32:44.867 --> 00:32:45.735
Thanks.

00:32:46.769 --> 00:32:47.637
Bye.

00:32:48.237 --> 00:32:49.105
Bye.

00:32:50.473 --> 00:32:52.475
Are you going to buy a house?

00:32:52.542 --> 00:32:53.876
-Huh?
-With Saku.

00:32:55.745 --> 00:32:57.346
I thought it could become the "clamp".

00:32:57.413 --> 00:32:58.381
Clamp?

00:32:58.448 --> 00:33:01.250
Something for us
so we can be together forever.

00:33:01.317 --> 00:33:04.754
Well, I know we’re not even dating yet,
so I know it sounds crazy.

00:33:07.323 --> 00:33:09.158
Let me know when you buy a house.

00:33:09.826 --> 00:33:11.227
Why?

00:33:11.294 --> 00:33:13.796
You two have zero talent

00:33:13.863 --> 00:33:15.364
for putting together furniture.

00:33:15.998 --> 00:33:17.166
I’ll come help again.

00:33:18.267 --> 00:33:19.502
And eat pizza together again?

00:33:19.569 --> 00:33:22.705
Yeah. I don’t really order pizza alone.

00:33:23.906 --> 00:33:26.309
-Alright.
-Okay, see you.

00:33:27.243 --> 00:33:28.277
See you.

00:33:35.084 --> 00:33:37.687
I'm fine now.
I can manage the rest myself.

00:33:37.753 --> 00:33:39.055
Don’t you need some of this?

00:33:39.122 --> 00:33:40.890
These are just things I don't use anymore.

00:33:40.957 --> 00:33:42.758
Doesn’t the room feel too bare

00:33:42.825 --> 00:33:44.127
and uncomfortable?

00:33:50.066 --> 00:33:51.100
‎FIRST LOVE

00:33:51.167 --> 00:33:52.201
What's this?

00:33:52.268 --> 00:33:53.503
Oh, that's…

00:33:55.037 --> 00:33:56.272
Did you make it yourself?

00:33:56.339 --> 00:33:59.041
Yeah. It was the first song I ever wrote
back in middle school.

00:33:59.108 --> 00:34:00.810
I want to hear it.

00:34:00.877 --> 00:34:04.213
No way… It's too embarrassing.

00:34:04.280 --> 00:34:05.615
What’s it about?

00:34:05.681 --> 00:34:08.351
It’s exactly what it says.

00:34:08.417 --> 00:34:09.852
A song about first love.

00:34:10.887 --> 00:34:13.589
You know I mentioned that guy, Koito?

00:34:14.757 --> 00:34:16.826
I liked him so much back in middle school,

00:34:16.893 --> 00:34:20.897
but when we were
always together as friends

00:34:20.963 --> 00:34:22.632
and we were teased for that,

00:34:22.698 --> 00:34:25.034
I was way too scared of getting caught,

00:34:25.101 --> 00:34:26.369
so I went along with it

00:34:27.336 --> 00:34:29.405
and said things like,
"Don't touch me, gay!"

00:34:30.573 --> 00:34:33.009
Fact is though,
I really wanted to touch him.

00:34:33.075 --> 00:34:34.043
Well,

00:34:34.544 --> 00:34:37.346
if you ever feel like singing,
I’ll listen anytime.

00:34:37.413 --> 00:34:38.814
Come on, now.

00:34:39.882 --> 00:34:40.716
No way.

00:34:44.153 --> 00:34:45.755
-Welcome back.
-Welcome back.

00:34:45.821 --> 00:34:47.223
You’re late. Where have you been?

00:34:47.290 --> 00:34:49.358
Koinobori was helping me with my studies.

00:34:49.926 --> 00:34:51.460
-Koinobori?
-Who's that?

00:34:51.961 --> 00:34:53.629
Anyway, I’m off to study now.

00:34:56.465 --> 00:34:58.601
Middle schoolers sometimes…

00:34:58.668 --> 00:35:00.203
I just don’t get them.

00:35:09.478 --> 00:35:10.313
It came out…

00:35:10.379 --> 00:35:12.682
When the Moon passes
between the Earth and the Sun

00:35:12.748 --> 00:35:15.318
and the Sun is completely hidden
by the Moon,

00:35:15.384 --> 00:35:17.153
what’s that phenomenon…?

00:35:18.988 --> 00:35:21.524
What was it again?

00:35:29.031 --> 00:35:31.467
END-OF-TERM EXAM
HOTARU KUSUNOKI

00:35:45.681 --> 00:35:47.683
Sorry, do you have a moment?

00:35:48.884 --> 00:35:52.355
-Yes?
-I was supposed to give back the tests,

00:35:52.421 --> 00:35:54.290
but Hotaru didn't come to school today.

00:35:54.357 --> 00:35:55.191
-What?
-Here.

00:35:55.825 --> 00:35:58.327
-Could you pass it to her?
-Okay.

00:35:59.395 --> 00:36:00.563
Tell her she did well.

00:36:01.864 --> 00:36:03.766
-Did she score well?
-See you.

00:36:06.869 --> 00:36:07.837
See you.

00:36:15.144 --> 00:36:16.712
Is this praiseworthy though?

00:36:16.779 --> 00:36:17.680
SECOND-TERM FINALS

00:36:20.816 --> 00:36:24.086
"When the Moon passes
between the Earth and the Sun…"

00:36:24.153 --> 00:36:25.221
Wait, isn't this…

00:36:28.524 --> 00:36:30.660
DESPAIR, RIDICULOUSLY FAR-OFF YEAR
TO LIVE

00:36:30.726 --> 00:36:31.861
This is no good then.

00:36:33.796 --> 00:36:35.331
"Revolution". Nice.

00:36:43.773 --> 00:36:44.874
"Despair"?

00:36:45.708 --> 00:36:47.009
Sure.

00:36:48.611 --> 00:36:51.147
But "in some ridiculously far-off year",

00:36:52.181 --> 00:36:54.250
I'm sure things will "get better",

00:36:55.551 --> 00:36:56.886
so I have to keep "being alive".

00:36:59.388 --> 00:37:00.656
"Keep going!"

00:37:06.362 --> 00:37:08.297
"Despair? Sure.

00:37:08.364 --> 00:37:10.232
But in some ridiculously far-off year,

00:37:10.299 --> 00:37:11.967
I'm sure things will get better,

00:37:12.468 --> 00:37:13.636
so I have to keep being alive."

00:37:14.737 --> 00:37:15.771
"Keep going!"

00:37:19.508 --> 00:37:20.676
Keep it up!

00:37:21.711 --> 00:37:24.146
KEEP GOING

00:37:29.752 --> 00:37:30.786
Welcome back.

00:37:32.455 --> 00:37:33.289
What do you want?

00:37:35.791 --> 00:37:38.127
This was entrusted to me by Mr. Sakuta.

00:37:40.429 --> 00:37:41.564
He said to pass it to you.

00:37:42.264 --> 00:37:44.066
Okay, goodnight.

00:37:45.134 --> 00:37:46.602
Goodnight.

00:37:56.746 --> 00:37:58.280
Can't believe he scribbled on it.

00:37:58.347 --> 00:37:59.615
KEEP GOING
YOU DID WELL

00:38:28.377 --> 00:38:31.180
‎SAITAMA PREFECTURE

00:38:40.689 --> 00:38:43.359
THIS IS WHAT I WANTED, WHAT I LOVE
AND WHAT I CHOSE FOR MYSELF

00:39:17.026 --> 00:39:18.394
Was I being too loud?

00:39:18.928 --> 00:39:19.762
No.

00:39:21.163 --> 00:39:22.898
The dogs were asleep,

00:39:22.965 --> 00:39:25.267
so I didn’t want to wake them.

00:39:25.334 --> 00:39:26.402
Right.

00:39:34.877 --> 00:39:35.778
Usually…

00:39:36.378 --> 00:39:39.048
I sing to relieve stress,

00:39:39.114 --> 00:39:41.617
but I guess even when I’m happy,
I do it too.

00:39:42.485 --> 00:39:44.253
Did something happy happen?

00:39:45.187 --> 00:39:46.222
Her test.

00:39:48.924 --> 00:39:50.059
Want to hear it?

00:39:50.125 --> 00:39:51.093
Yeah.

00:39:57.233 --> 00:40:01.804
Today my heart

00:40:02.304 --> 00:40:05.975
Tucked in the bottom of my bag

00:40:06.976 --> 00:40:11.547
Hidden away

00:40:11.614 --> 00:40:15.251
So no one sees

00:40:16.385 --> 00:40:20.656
Tomorrow it’ll rest

00:40:21.223 --> 00:40:24.126
Deep inside my pocket

00:40:25.928 --> 00:40:30.432
Might slip right out

00:40:30.499 --> 00:40:34.370
If I’m not careful

00:40:38.507 --> 00:40:42.211
I’m sure it’s not love

00:40:43.045 --> 00:40:47.216
It can’t be, it’s different
From everyone else.

00:40:47.783 --> 00:40:51.387
I’m sure it’s not love

00:40:51.453 --> 00:40:55.858
So I’ll just leave it here and say goodbye

00:40:55.925 --> 00:40:58.060
After the beep tone,

00:40:58.127 --> 00:41:00.896
please leave your name and message.

00:41:01.430 --> 00:41:02.965
Hello, Hotaru?

00:41:03.566 --> 00:41:04.967
It's been a while.

00:41:05.034 --> 00:41:06.835
I’ve been listening to your voicemails.

00:41:07.369 --> 00:41:09.305
Doesn’t feel fair
for only you to reach out,

00:41:09.371 --> 00:41:13.375
so I thought maybe I’d talk a little
about what’s been going on with me lately.

00:41:14.076 --> 00:41:16.178
This has to be a mistake, right?

00:41:16.245 --> 00:41:17.546
Oh, sorry about that.

00:41:17.613 --> 00:41:19.915
It’s a 15-minute walk, not 15 hours.

00:41:19.982 --> 00:41:23.752
The other day, I met this young woman
who's planning to buy a condo.

00:41:23.819 --> 00:41:25.854
Could you tell me
why you’re buying the condo?

00:41:25.921 --> 00:41:27.489
I don’t want to be looked down on.

00:41:28.557 --> 00:41:30.726
I want people to think I’m cool.

00:41:30.793 --> 00:41:32.127
‎Oh, no.

00:41:32.194 --> 00:41:33.729
That’s not what I meant.

00:41:34.530 --> 00:41:36.966
She kind of reminded me of you, Hotaru.

00:41:37.032 --> 00:41:38.334
She was working so hard.

00:41:45.541 --> 00:41:49.244
She was really giving it her all,
trying to buy something she truly wanted.

00:41:51.981 --> 00:41:53.816
‎INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

00:41:53.882 --> 00:41:54.850
Hotaru,

00:41:55.517 --> 00:41:57.353
no matter what kind of adult you become,

00:41:57.853 --> 00:41:59.521
I just hope that, by then,

00:41:59.588 --> 00:42:02.224
the world will be a place

00:42:02.291 --> 00:42:04.660
where you don’t have to feel sad anymore.

00:42:06.962 --> 00:42:08.097
Okay then.

00:42:08.697 --> 00:42:09.665
Talk to you soon.

00:42:12.468 --> 00:42:13.435
Is that "First Love"?

00:42:13.502 --> 00:42:16.071
Yeah. Since I found the tape,

00:42:16.138 --> 00:42:17.973
and it’s been a while
since I heard the name.

00:42:18.040 --> 00:42:19.041
Whose name?

00:42:19.108 --> 00:42:21.910
Hotaru mentioned the name
Koinobori the other day.

00:42:22.544 --> 00:42:25.714
Koito's name is written with the kanji
for Koinobori,

00:42:25.781 --> 00:42:26.982
but read as Koito.

00:42:27.049 --> 00:42:29.718
Everyone used to call him Koinobori.

00:42:29.785 --> 00:42:32.087
I doubt it's really him though.

00:42:32.154 --> 00:42:33.689
Aren’t you going to see for yourself?

00:42:34.723 --> 00:42:36.325
Oh, no. That’d be…

00:42:36.925 --> 00:42:37.860
cruel.

00:42:49.438 --> 00:42:50.606
You're not a dog, you know?

00:42:52.441 --> 00:42:54.376
Don't give me a "shake" or "paw".

00:42:56.445 --> 00:42:57.579
Then…

00:42:58.781 --> 00:42:59.615
Like this.

00:43:03.018 --> 00:43:04.086
Okay.

00:43:18.167 --> 00:43:19.368
I did bring true mirin.

00:43:20.636 --> 00:43:22.371
Thank you.

00:43:23.706 --> 00:43:26.041
Mr. Koi… Koinobori?

00:43:26.875 --> 00:43:30.112
It's Koito. It's written as Koinobori,
but read as Koito.

00:43:31.313 --> 00:43:32.748
Here. That way.

00:43:33.949 --> 00:43:35.617
Thank you, Mr. Koito.

00:43:35.684 --> 00:43:36.985
You're welcome.

00:43:38.020 --> 00:43:40.222
TRUE MIRIN

00:43:41.790 --> 00:43:44.460
-May I have some next?
-Oh, sure.

00:43:54.336 --> 00:43:55.537
You know,

00:43:56.305 --> 00:43:57.773
maybe I should go see him.

00:44:01.376 --> 00:44:02.311
Koito.

00:44:05.814 --> 00:44:07.883
Are you seriously…

00:44:07.950 --> 00:44:10.519
saying that in this situation?

00:45:52.354 --> 00:45:54.256
Subtitle translation by: Jeffery